+ * goals the talking agent never sees. The owning process appends to this log,
+ * and both processes share it on disk.
+ *
+ * The ACP session id is the `<sessionId>` directory name, so the log path is
+ * derivable from the id the daemon already holds.
+ */
+
+/**
+ * Polling cadences. The two fastest were slowed down after a hang where the
+ * daemon stopped answering on its port while the process stayed alive: each poll
+ * read and parsed everything appended since the last one, so the per-tick cost
+ * was unbounded and the main thread could be held for as long as the log had
+ * grown. The reads are now budgeted and the parse yields (see below); a slower
+ * cadence keeps the number of those bounded ticks down.
