+ * while a live session appends a few kilobytes per step — so this is orders of
+ * magnitude more than one cadence needs and the budget only binds while catching
+ * up on a long pre-existing log. The upper end of that range is the right one
+ * because the budget also sets catch-up throughput (budget per active cadence),
+ * and a cold replay starts at byte 0.
